10:30:15 the card opened with MTestZ1 already in drive alarm A.A12 (EtherCAT Output Data Synchronization Error) / ERROR_STOP. The other
18 axes get golden's boot InitMotor (with ResetError); MTestZ1 is left out of kBootInitAxes on purpose (golden's InitMotor on it is
TMyGALILMotor::InitMotor = no-op; the Galil route servos it ON at HOME, "SH"), so nothing cleared it until EastSun pressed Reset on
the 1203 page (10:32:34). Now, once per run after the same 1 s motor-power gate: an enabled, opened PCI1203 MTestZ1 whose sample
shows an alarm (MotionIO ALM or ERROR_STOP) gets ONE Acm_AxResetError -- the same command as Motor Test / 1203 page Alarm Reset.
No servo-on, no CFG write, no motion; logged as a BRAKE line. No ctest compiles WebMotorAccessLive.cpp; verify by the op log line
"MTestZ1 boot alarm reset" on the next start. Debug wb_serve built. WORKLOG row 215.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
